the West is believed that Iran has had a  clandestine nuclear weapons program for  well over a decade the most visible  aspects of that program are its  facilities to enrich uranium the uranium  has to be put into a chemical form that  can be fed into the centrifuges that  process is called conversion uranium  hexafluoride goes into the centrifuges  the centrifuges spin around at a very  high rate and that separates out the  different isotopes of uranium if they  continue that process they will  eventually get highly enriched uranium  in gaseous form that material then has  to be reconverted into solid form once  that is done then the bomb has to be  assembled and that is a very complex  design task if Iran were to operate its  enrichment capability at maximum  potential it could have enough isle  enriched uranium to make a bomb in a few  months there's really no good defense  against a nuclear weapons attack the  flight time for a ballistic missile from  Iran to for example Tel Aviv would be  just a few minutes and it's one of the  reasons why the original acquisition of  nuclear weapons is so objectionable to  the international community
 

